# API workflow

Work from the contract, in order.

1. Read the lowest unchecked task in `docs/backend-tasks.md` (or `../docs/backend-tasks.md`).
2. Change only the files that task names.
3. Add the listed unit test first when the task gives concrete cases.
4. From the API root run, in order, every script that exists: `npm run format:check`, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build`.
5. Commit with `docs/commit-guidelines.md` only after that gate is green: `type(scope): subject`, subject under 50 characters. One task, one commit. Do not start the next task.

Load `implement-api-task` before feature work. Load `stay-on-contract` when a field, status, message, or library call is not already written in the task or the LLD. Do not invent it.

Stack: Node 22, Express, TypeScript strict, NodeNext, Mongoose, Zod, argon2, jsonwebtoken, pino, Temporal, Vitest. Verify with `npm test` and `npm run typecheck` from the API root.
